.TH TARIFE 1 "2026-09-08" "realisateur" "bashified verb"
.SH NAME
tarife \- price this tree against the estate's guards, before you push
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tarife
.br
.B tarife
--gate
.br
.B tarife
--refresh
.br
.B tarife
--quiet
.SH DESCRIPTION
Runs the guards that grade a pull request, against the working tree, so their
verdict arrives in the terminal instead of five minutes later in CI.
.PP
The prose ratchet and the state-prose lint are
.B hf7y/etalon's
and are never copied here. They are fetched by reference and executed from a
cache under
.IR $XDG_CACHE_HOME/etalon-guards ,
which is what CI does when it checks etalon out into
.IR .etalon :
a different runner, not a vendored copy.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --gate
Only the guards fast enough to run at every turn end: the prose ratchet and the
state-prose lint. Skips shellcheck, which is 88s on realisateur's tree. An
unchanged tree exits immediately \- the result is fingerprinted on HEAD plus the
working diff, so re-running costs nothing.
.TP
.B --refresh
Re-fetch the guards even if the cache is warm. The cache otherwise refreshes on
a 12-hour TTL.
.TP
.B --quiet
Print findings only.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Every guard passed.
.TP
.B 1
A guard found something. Its own output says what, and what to do about it.
.TP
.B 6
BLIND \- a guard could not be fetched and no cached copy exists. Never folded
into 0.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B TARIFE_CACHE
Where the fetched guards live. Default
.IR ${XDG_CACHE_HOME:-$HOME/.cache}/etalon-guards .
.TP
.B TARIFE_TTL_MIN
Minutes before a cached guard is re-fetched. Default 720.
.SH NOTES
A stale cache still answers. The guards change rarely, and a ratchet a day out
of date still tells you that you added prose; refusing to run offline would make
this useless exactly where it is most needed.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR reap (1)
is what the ratchet tells you to run, and it asks for twice the deficit \- the
tree is full of prose that outlived its mechanism, and paying the deficit
exactly leaves the tree where it was.
